  "details": "I am just getting into learning all of this audio stuff and as it seems unity supports different channels of audio on 1 track for a 5.1, 7.1 or beyond experience. Which you can do if you had the video and audio in unity and set it up. However when streaming from a server it seems like VRC limits this by only letting you do Stereo Mixes or mono. I'm not entirely sure how audio transfers over from a link to VRC_Video Stream to the speakers but if this was possible it would make watching videos in VR way more immersive rather than just having stereo 2d audio at your center when there could be more.",
